# PowerShell Command Chaining

The shell is **PowerShell on Windows**. `&&` is not a valid statement separator.

## Rule

Always use `;` to chain commands — never `&&`.

```powershell
# ❌ BAD — breaks in PowerShell
cd my-project && python -m tools manifest

# ✅ GOOD
cd my-project; python -m tools manifest
```

This applies to every shell command in every response, with no exceptions.
